WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.950
A seaside resort on a southern island...

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.990
We can forget all about
puzzles and just relax.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.200
Everyone, here goes!

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.830
Ha-yaa!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.500
At least, that's what I'd imagined...

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.660
All right!

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.790
I win again.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.680
Don't think this luck
of yours is gonna last!

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.430
Thirty seconds have elapsed!

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.560
Solved it!

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.160
I, Ana, too!

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.120
Goodness, what are you doing, Galileo?!

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:45.500
I..It's the puzzle!
Goodness, what are you doing, Galileo?!

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.410
I..It's the puzzle!
You're out of time!

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.520
It's messed up!
You're out of time!

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.370
I swear!

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:54.030
Why am I even here?

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.000
Lost

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.130
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.050
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.970
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.310
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.020
Found

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.270
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:33.730
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.570
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.660
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.990
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.910
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.620
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.960
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.170
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.550
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.010
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:58.720
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.550
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.430
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.560
It's now or never

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.640
That is what they say

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.730
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.400
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.570
That is what they say

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:15.730
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.240
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.450
That is what they say

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.870
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.080
Even Nonoha Wants to Solve Them!

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:34.980
Puzzle Drill Camp: Days Left - 4

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.540
I came here thinking we'd have a
blow-out great time together.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.370
But now that it's a "camp,"
I have nothing to do.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:57.780
On top of that...

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.320
I feel like my puzzle-solving abilities

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.560
are getting better and better!

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.830
Me, too!

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.160
It's quite promising.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.160
Well, our "queen" is pretty demanding.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:11.960
Just as long as you're grateful.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.370
The way we are now,

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:17.640
the Orpheus Order would
have no chance at all, huh?

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.260
Not at all, not at all!

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.130
Glad to hear it.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.590
We're countin' on you two.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.780
Oh, they're counting on us!

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.560
Why are you teasing us?

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.290
I ain't teasin' ya.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.640
Never mind Kaito and Gammon;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.090
even Cube and Ana seem to be having fun,

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.610
and they didn't like puzzles at first.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.060
Sir, I tried grinding a

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.920
little apple into your curry
as a secret ingredient.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.520
Do you like it?

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.010
And yet, I...

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:50.450
So that's your trick, huh?

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.250
Then, what do you say to this?

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.340
In that case, I-

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.290
Kaito! Gammon!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.170
No puzzles while you're eating!

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.030
Cube!

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.880
No computing while you're eating!

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.590
Ana, no drawing!

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.930
I'm confiscating all of this!

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.390
These are off limits while you're eating.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.510
But I have to input that puzzle design.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.650
My imagination was running
explosively wild!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.610
Give it back!

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.990
That's right, this is
a man-to-man contest!

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.990
You're still talkin' back?!

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.780
Nonoha, you fiend!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.980
You devil!

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.350
Fiend!

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.830
Devil!

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.330
Shut up!

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.410
Come on, Brother!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.830
Miss Itou, don't you go rampaging
while we're eating either!

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:37.660
Honestly, this is so raucous.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:39.420
They're all quite energetic, aren't they?
Honestly, this is so raucous.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.370
It's gonna spill!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.760
Whose turn is it to go shopping tomorrow?

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:50.680
Oh, it's mine!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.560
Then, it will be mine tomorrow,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.170
Itou's the day after that,

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.920
and Mizutani on the last day, please.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.020
Okay!

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.030
Miss Nonoha, your sweets
are so delicious!

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.910
Your cooking is the best.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.780
You've been such a help
since you've been here!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.680
Thank you.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.410
Maybe I could have fun with the others

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.890
if I could solve puzzles too.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.120
Huh? A present?

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.760
Yeah, close your eyes
and hold out your hands.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.120
Like this?

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.080
You can open your eyes.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.570
Ta-daa!

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:12.510
Jeez, you know I'm no good at puzzles!

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:16.750
If you don't like it, just solve it!

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.090
Hey, Kaito!

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.320
All right!

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:28.320
And so...

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.320
As of today, I'll do your
puzzle training too!

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.790
What're you talkin' about?

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.160
Ain't no way you can do that!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.760
I won't know unless I try, will I?

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.170
No, I know.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:43.980
Well, where's the harm?

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:45.220
Hey, Erena!

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:45.960
For real?

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:47.740
All right!

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.430
Thank you, Erena!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.430
Keep up with us, if you can.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.640
You have ten minutes,

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.230
and one hundred puzzle rings.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:58.930
Okay, start!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.950
You have ten minutes,

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:16.060
and two hundred wooden cross puzzles.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.790
Okay, start!

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:28.960
Um... Um... Um...

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.780
Pull three hundred sticks without
letting the pile collapse.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.590
Okay, start!

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:40.310
Um, three hundred...

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.460
Erena?

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.420
What?

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.090
I'm thirsty.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:53.070
Do you have some water or something?

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.110
I have to solve a puzzle?

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.120
Yes.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:03.170
I'm hungry...

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.380
I knew it.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.570
Bathroom, bathroom!

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:09.460
Huh?

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.270
For real?

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.040
Look, just give up and get some lunch!

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.320
No way.

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:40.820
Why did you suddenly say
you want to join in the training?

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:43.070
"Why?"

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:46.290
The Orpheus Order seems pretty tough,

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.160
and I thought if I could
solve puzzles too,

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.990
I could be of help.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:50.960
Sort of.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.570
Okay, Antoinette.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:55.780
We gotta exercise to help us digest!

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.760
Let's go on to the next puzzle.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:02.270
Seriously, all you do is
eat and solve puzzles.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.920
What's that?

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:12.900
A maze?

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:14.650
This maze!

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.050
It's Minotaur's!

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.510
The one that was behind the academy?

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:24.750
Whoa, she's right.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:28.660
You can do all Philosopher's Puzzles
and Puzzles of Fools.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:32.500
After all, those puzzles
had already been solved.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.450
Let me do it!

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:35.010
Nonoha!

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.980
You snooze, you lose!

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:39.940
Jeez!

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.910
Where's the harm?

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.600
Nonoha will crash and burn...

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:45.980
NOT!

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.610
That's some crazy speed!

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:57.110
This is...

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.870
that Devil's Handmaiden's puzzle!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.370
Great job!

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.540
Nonoha's solvin' puzzles?!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.610
It's nothing to be shocked about.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:14.300
Did you forget about Nonoha's memory?

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.050
Her memory?

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.050
If she sees somethin' once,
she won't never forget it.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.810
She ain't solving puzzles;

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.590
she's just reusing puzzle-solving
techniques she's seen before.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:29.060
Erena's miniature puzzle!

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:31.650
Back then, Kaito...

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:42.450
This puzzle is...

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.170
Huh?

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.680
What? What's this?

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:08.130
Oh, jeez, I messed up!

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.380
Why'd you suddenly crap out?

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:12.650
When I solved that puzzle,

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.440
Nonoha wasn't there.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.760
I had a good run, didn't I?

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.310
If I try, I can do it!

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.200
Quit forcin' yourself to do puzzles!

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:25.730
It's all right.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:28.950
No matter what puzzle the
Orpheus Order throws at us,

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:31.330
we'll solve 'em all!

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:32.940
"We"?

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:37.460
Yeah, leave it to us, and there
ain't nothin' to worry about!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.950
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.500
You're all here.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.970
You're all good at puzzles.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:52.000
I don't know about "all" of us, though.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.100
Yeah, got that right!

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.110
I can't be one of you all...

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.150
Huh? You say something?

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.300
I'm going back.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:04.470
Huh?!

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:07.330
I shouldn't try what I'm not good at.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.530
My brain's tired too.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:13.120
I'll make dinner, so
I'm heading back early.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:14.600
See ya.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.010
Yeah!

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:19.850
Nonoha's actin' kinda
strange, don't you think?

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:20.760
Really?

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:46.680
It's all right.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:49.890
No matter what puzzle the
Orpheus Order throws at us,

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:52.370
we'll solve 'em all!

00:12:57.050 --> 00:13:00.300
I can't...

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:04.300
If you don't like it, just solve it!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:08.430
No, I can't give up.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:09.720
First, I start here.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:13.050
By the time this camp is done,

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:14.980
I will have solved this puzzle.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.010
Okay, sorry for the wait!

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.890
Miss Vice Prez gets a rice omelet.

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:19.720
Thank you.

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:22.390
Upperclassman Jikukawa
gets apple stir-fry.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:23.570
Thank you.

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:26.380
Look, Miharu!

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:30.260
This is my special, tons
o' seafood fried noodles.

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:33.010
Thanks very much.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:44.970
Everyone, don't do other
things while you're eating!

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.100
A'aight.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:47.930
Okaaaaay.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.760
A little longer.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:54.260
Sakanoue, It's all right to
look out for your sister,

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:56.640
but eat your own food too!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:00.180
C'mon, Miharu, say "Aaaah!"

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.970
I said I can do it on my own!

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:04.190
I swear...

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.180
Quite the handful, aren't they?

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:07.680
What happened to Nonoha?

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.140
Erekawa!

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:11.800
Address your upperclassman
as "Miss Itou"!

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.080
Um, where's Miss Itou?

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:19.170
She said she had something to do,
so she'll be eating in her room.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:21.240
Something to do?

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:38.690
Puzzle Drill Camp: Days Left - 3

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.100
The next one's white, so, uh...

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.930
Twenty seconds left.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.540
Come on, go more to the left!

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:49.020
Yeah, I know!

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:49.950
Shut up, already!

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.500
This probably goes on the corner, right?

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.950
One minute left!

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:15.970
Puzzle Drill Camp: Days Left - 2

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:24.030
Come on, Miharu!

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:26.190
I said, I can do it myself!

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.460
This atmosphere's gotten sort of...

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:34.240
President, aren't Daimon and
the others acting strange?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:39.750
Cubik and Ana don't even
leave their rooms anymore.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.750
That's right.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.520
Wonder what's happened, huh?

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:55.520
What? Why'd you call me out here?

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.350
I'm the one who has questions.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.800
Just what are you doing all alone?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.740
The truth is...

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.360
Huh? A puzzle?

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:08.360
Yes.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:12.000
I'm determined to finish
it before camp is over.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.160
Because you want to be useful?

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:18.850
No...

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.540
It looks like I don't belong anywhere.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:28.720
I mean, everyone is bound
by puzzles, but not me.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.510
You don't get it...

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:36.850
So, if you do solve that
puzzle, what's your intention?

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.350
I'm asking you, if you
don't belong anywhere

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.690
and you can't solve
that puzzle, then what?

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.420
If I can't solve it...

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:55.450
If I can't solve it, I can't
remain with the others.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:07.960
Puzzle Drill Camp: Days Left - 1

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.630
Kaito is absorbed puzzles,

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:17.240
Cubik is doing some kind of research,

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.260
Ana is painting something,

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.930
and Gammon is pretty hands-on,

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.980
so he and Miharu went somewhere alone.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.950
Sir!

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:32.740
Quite the handful, aren't they?

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:52.430
I will...

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:54.890
I will...

00:17:57.270 --> 00:17:58.390
solve this!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.570
Sure enough, I couldn't solve it.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.590
Nonoha...

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.130
What's wrong? Airi?

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.980
There's nothing to make breakfast with.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:50.530
Yesterday was my turn to get groceries,

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:54.180
but I got distracted by housewares

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:56.860
and forgot to buy the groceries.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:01.120
Even if we went to town now,
we wouldn't make it in time.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.100
If upperclassmen Kaito and Gammon

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:08.480
have to go without breakfast,
they'll be mad at me!

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.250
Please help me, Ma'am!

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:12.820
Please help!

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:16.240
We don't know what to do...

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:31.300
Miharu, go see if there aren't any eggs

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:33.660
left in the last box down there.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.600
Airi, check the fridge.

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:37.480
We should still have ham and butter.

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.270
Ma'am!

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:45.370
We have some!

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:48.870
We have supplies here too!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.750
Here, there's pasta.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.750
And here, a full range of seasonings.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:56.370
Good morning.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:57.250
What's going on?

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:00.230
Upperclassman Jikukawa!
Miss Vice President!

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:02.210
We have some potatoes in the rear fridge.

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:03.670
Could you get them for me?

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:05.880
Huh? Uh, okay.

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:08.140
Miss Erena, help me.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:11.270
No need for "Miss."

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:20.460
Kaito!

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:22.610
Kaito!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.930
Get the hell up!

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:27.830
Uncle! Uncle, uncle!
Get the hell up!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.790
Gammon, get the hell up!

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:36.940
Hurry and get dressed.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.090
Ma'am.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.250
Stop it, Nonoha!

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:43.070
I'm at a good point with my research!

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:45.950
I, Ana, just had a breakthrough too.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:48.060
Enough, we're all eating
breakfast together!

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.360
How 'bout this?!

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.160
What's that?

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.180
Kaito! Gammon!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.250
No puzzles while you're eating!

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:08.450
Cube, you neither!

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.320
Ana, you neither!

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.700
Confiscated!

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:15.450
Nonoha, you fiend! You devil!

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:17.680
Fiend! Devil!

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:19.590
Shut it and start eating!

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.670
Miss Vice President...

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:25.920
Yes, they've gone back
to their usual selves.

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:27.970
Sir, what's going on?

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:31.040
Yes, what, indeed?

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.230
Off limits till
you're done eating!!

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:38.700
So, my brother always-

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:39.880
Nonoha...

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.480
Did you solve that puzzle?

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:44.150
W..Well...

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:48.030
If you couldn't solve it,
you can't remain with them, wasn't it?

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.150
I can't do puzzles,

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:54.840
but I've decided to do what I can do.

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:59.040
To make my own place where I belong.

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:02.050
Sure enough, you don't get it.

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:04.020
Huh? Get what?

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:06.020
I won't say; won't tell you.

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:09.850
Now you've friggin' done it!

00:22:09.850 --> 00:22:11.360
What's wrong, Gammon?

00:22:11.360 --> 00:22:12.820
It's your turn.

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:14.960
M..My...

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.190 --> 00:24:03.870
Hello, Souji Jikukawa.

00:24:03.870 --> 00:24:05.060
It's been a while.

00:24:05.060 --> 00:24:07.340
It's me, Minotaur.

00:24:07.340 --> 00:24:09.840
Your puzzle-solving skill
is splendid, as always.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:13.830
I have prepared a splendid game for you.

00:24:13.830 --> 00:24:15.190
Don't you want to know?

00:24:15.190 --> 00:24:17.150
About the true Phi-Brain?

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:20.100
Next time, "Minotaur's Lure"

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:23.350
Come, let puzzle time begin,

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:26.670
Minotaur's Lure

00:24:23.350 --> 00:24:25.560
Newton aka Souji Jikukawa.
